{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cca3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa23-c753-7e20-ba14-a3c953f652a1"},"sequence":1196,"recorded_at":1780531400002387,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"60ee70b2-d33d-438c-9a26-1cd548916052","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"60ee70b2-d33d-438c-9a26-1cd548916052","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"60ee70b2-d33d-438c-9a26-1cd548916052"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Ready for review — handed off to review.\n\nCR rev1 failed its own gate at `validation-contract-tests` (exit 1, empty inner log). I separated the two causes: mise-trust stderr noise, which is harmless under `set -u` and is now gone after trusting the brief-authorized `tuist 4.202.5` config, and the real failure — the rev1 runner move tripped the in-repo contract still pinning `runs-on: macos-15`. I reproduced that exit-1/0-byte failure, then updated that one expectation to `macos-26` (checksum, pin, and ordering assertions untouched) and wired the native-toolchain suite plus its mutant harness into the existing contract lane, per the parent directive confirming both as in-scope.\n\nThe rev1 four-path delta is byte-identical (all blobs re-verified) and the 59-path prerequisite overlay is byte-equal to PR6 head `d45c85d`; HEAD is unmoved and nothing is committed. Prospective composition is now PR6 head + 5 paths, with identities in the new outcome `BUG-260916-1rqn1c_results-rev2.md`.\n\nValidation, all with exact exit codes: contract step exit 0 (12/12 alignment, both mutant harnesses killing all mutants), full `make credential-free-validate` exit 0 with all 17 stages PASS, `make check-native-dependencies` exit 0, Xcode 26.6 negative proof exit 1 with the strict mismatch message, YAML parse and `git diff --check` clean, `xcode-select` untouched. AC coverage is 4 of 6 rows driven through the production entry; review and hosted publication/landing remain stated bounds, and hosted green still requires the parent to publish the prospective PR.","reason":null}}
